  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1409.02 Requirements for Used Oil Burners",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1409.02 Requirements for Used Oil Burners. Used oil burners shall comply with the requirements of Env-Hw 1405 and, as applicable:\n\n(a) Env-Hw 1409.03 through Env-Hw 1409.09;\n\n(b) Env-A 1600 for fuel specifications and Env-A 2000 for fuel burning devices;\n\n(c) Env-Hw 1406 for generating used oil;\n\n(d) Env-Hw 1407 for transporting used oil and operating a used oil transfer facility;\n\n(e) Env-Hw 1408 for processing or re-refining used oil, except as provided under Env-Hw 1409.04(b); and\n\n(f) Env-Hw 1410 for acting as a used oil fuel marketer.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
